{"thought": "Harper named Friday, Oct 16 at 4:15 pm, and the booking card for that slot is drafted. But Harper already has a confirmed Kickoff call on Wed, Oct 21 at 9:45 am, so approving this card would give Harper two calls. That is Bob's decision, so I'm telling him rather than assuming.", "tool": "tell_bob", "args": {"text": "Harper Quill wrote back that Friday, Oct 16 at 4:15 pm is on their calendar, and that time is free on your side. The card as drafted books a 45-minute Kickoff call with Harper Quill, Fri Oct 16, 4:15 to 5:00 pm. Your required colleague is invited automatically, and Sasha is invited as optional. Nothing reaches anyone until you tap Approve.

The problem is that an earlier Kickoff call with Harper, Wed Oct 21 at 9:45 to 10:30 am, was already booked and confirmed on your approval. Harper's last message may be about that invite, or may not. If you approve this card, Harper would have two calls, and I can't cancel the Wednesday one.

Which should stand: the Friday 4:15 call (approve the card, then cancel Wednesday yourself), or the Wednesday 9:45 call (I'll stop here and leave Friday unbooked)?"}}
